\section*{Computation by compactly supported eventually periodic box transport}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
\textit{Full-box transport and finite computation}: The paper claims effective incompressible realization of determinant-one positive diagonal maps on neighborhoods of entire solid rational boxes. A balanced recorder turns these maps into particle halting detection with fixed compact spatial support and eventually periodic forcing.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Mathematical claim 1.} For the incompressible system $\partial_tu+(u\cdot\nabla)u=-\nabla p+\nu\Delta u+f$, $\nabla\cdot u=0$, $u(0)=0$, choose viscosity $\nu>0$, whose value is computable. On $\mathbb R^3$, the construction supplies effective coefficients $f_0,f_1$ with $f=f_0+\nu f_1$ and an explicit zero-data solution $(U,0)$. Both fields vanish outside the same fixed compact spatial region, every mixed derivative is bounded, and both are period one after $t=1$. For the fixed particle $x_*=(4,0,0)$, \[\exists t\ge0:X(t;x_*)\in(-1,2)^3\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad M(w)\text{ halts}.\] The repeated mechanism depends only on the machine; uniqueness holds among $u\in CH^2\cap C^1L^2$ with $u,\nabla u$ bounded on any finite interval, and a $CH^1$ pressure representative after choosing its additive constant.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
\textit{Full-box transport and finite computation}: Localized curls evacuate overlapping source boxes into storage, deform them there, and deliver them along obstacle-avoiding detours. A three-stack recorder keeps the finite instruction system reversible. The construction checks observations at every intermediate time and derives effective derivative bounds, with separate torus and slow-clock variants treated under their stated comparison classes.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
\textit{Full-box transport and finite computation}: The box-transport realization has one fixed compact spatial support and an eventually periodic field with zero pressure. Its repeated mechanism can be fixed for a machine independently of its finite input, while initialization encodes the input and the detector checks the full continuous trajectory.

With the hypotheses and conventions above, the claimed result addresses the whole mathematical assertion on this page.

\subsection{Formal verification}
Family 376 describes Lean coverage for the selected sheet-program, rapidly decaying particle-detector, velocity-detector, and full-box transport statements described separately in its Comparator files.

\textit{Full-box transport and finite computation}: The manuscript links \texttt{BalancedBoxRouting.lean}, \texttt{BalancedThreeStack.lean}, \texttt{ForcedNavierStokesComputation.lean}, \texttt{NavierStokesAlternating.lean}, \texttt{NavierStokesVelocity.lean}, \texttt{SolenoidalSheetPrograms.lean}.

The documented selection includes this manuscript’s main assertion; that assertion retains the restrictions stated above.

This site has not run the Lean development. These links describe OpenAI’s selected formal statements and should be read with their stated scope.

